  "answer": "I found no past ticket that reports this exact problem. That problem is Burn detecting and planning each per-user related bundle twice, which leaves a stale Installed Apps entry with a missing cached EXE. Some tickets are close but not the same. PowerToys#42181 has the same 0x80070003 'Failed to configure per-user related bundle' non-vital error, but it is about a reinstall with a file-in-use failure, and it never mentions duplicate planning. PowerToys#43774, #47250 and #46994 show the duplicated i102 'Detected related bundle' lines. Their actual failure is the 0x81f40001 per-user versus per-machine conflict, which is a different problem. Please file this as a new installer issue. Include the full Burn logs, and link wixtoolset/issues#7675. To clear a stale entry now, you can try uninstalling the matching older bundle from its cached copy if one still exists, or use a per-user installer of the same version to repair and then remove it. I could not confirm that workaround from the archive."
 },
